        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-12T18:15:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you add some documentation on what values are expected here?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 36,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "4a4c23559ad0c3d1507bff9b3865544158d1c63e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3bc4f72d_a41ec012",
        "filename": "nfc/aidl/android/hardware/nfc/ProtocolDiscoveryConfig.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 36,
      "author": {
        "id": 1644679
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-12T18:20:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are these values in the NCI Spec as well? What guarantees do we have that they will never change (for backward compatibility requirements).",
      "parentUuid": "e37a02fc_fa138dfc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 36,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "4a4c23559ad0c3d1507bff9b3865544158d1c63e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "35b4c5be_e0fd0ace",
        "filename": "nfc/aidl/android/hardware/nfc/ProtocolDiscoveryConfig.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 36,
      "author": {
        "id": 1153044
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-13T10:36:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This value should be handled as the values for MIFARE, Kovio or PollBPrime. Chinese Id tags are non-compliant with NFC_forum and there is no documentation explaining it. The value used for the Chinese Id protocol can be anything as long as it is on the range defined by the NCI specification for the proprietary values (0x80 - 0xFE)",
      "parentUuid": "3bc4f72d_a41ec012",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 36,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "4a4c23559ad0c3d1507bff9b3865544158d1c63e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dfc362c3_6d920d8f",
        "filename": "nfc/aidl/android/hardware/nfc/ProtocolDiscoveryConfig.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 36,
      "author": {
        "id": 1644679
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-13T17:09:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These values are passed through the Android framework code without it trying to interpret the values?\n\nSorry, I\u0027m not familiar with this part of the interface, but we generally can\u0027t accept unknown values in the Android framework if it needs to reference/interpret those values because the framework needs to remain backward compatible with all HAL implementations.",
      "parentUuid": "35b4c5be_e0fd0ace",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 36,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "4a4c23559ad0c3d1507bff9b3865544158d1c63e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5936a050_c1888e1d",
        "filename": "nfc/aidl/android/hardware/nfc/ProtocolDiscoveryConfig.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 36,
      "author": {
        "id": 1153044
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-14T07:34:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As I explained in ticket 3083710: Reading of Chinese Id card | https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/system/nfc/+/3083710\nThis is an arbitrary value; it does not come from the ST NFCC. The FW will return \"unknown protocol, frame RF, poll B\" if a Chinese Id card is detected. For simplification, we translate that to a dedicated protocol value. This value is only used inside the system/nfc code, the JNI will see \"unknown protocol, frame RF, type B\", and it is also what will be broadcasted.",
      "parentUuid": "dfc362c3_6d920d8f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 36,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "4a4c23559ad0c3d1507bff9b3865544158d1c63e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3d77cc52_a31d1bab",
        "filename": "nfc/aidl/android/hardware/nfc/ProtocolDiscoveryConfig.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 36,
      "author": {
        "id": 1306902
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-14T08:31:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Byte values listed in ProtocolDiscoveryConfig are all vendor proprietary.\nVendor HAL implementation need to fill in these values based on their definition.\nFor example:\nIn NXP impl, protocolMifare is 0x80, but in ST\u0027s impl is 0x90.",
      "parentUuid": "5936a050_c1888e1d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 36,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "4a4c23559ad0c3d1507bff9b3865544158d1c63e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
